      {
        "location": "applications/github/.haiknow/acceptance.json:9621",
        "text": "\"description\": \"The organization overview page uses the organization name as a heading; its 鈥淩epositories鈥? 鈥淧eople鈥? and 鈥淭eams鈥?navigation entries have link roles even when visually styled as tabs. The Repositories tab lists repositories owned by the organization, the People tab lists members and their Member/Owner roles, and the Teams tab lists teams. This module supports visitors discovering an organization's public repositories and signed-in accounts creating organizations from the 鈥淵our or"
      },
      {
        "location": "applications/github/.haiknow/acceptance.json:9669",
        "text": "\"description\": \"On the current organization's member- and team-management pages, users create teams, maintain team hierarchy and membership relationships, and directly add or remove organization members. A team name contains 1鈥?0 lowercase ASCII letters, digits, or hyphens, may not begin or end with a hyphen, and must be unique within the same organization; a team must belong to an organization, and a parent team must belong to the same organization and may not create a direct or indirect cycle."
      },
      {
        "location": "applications/github/.haiknow/acceptance.json:9797",
        "text": "\"description\": \"The repository-creation page is the form opened by 鈥淣ew repository鈥? where the user selects an owner, name, visibility, and initialization options. A 鈥渇ork鈥?is an independent repository copied from a readable source repository 鈥?the frontend displays the source link on the fork overview page, and the system stores the source-repository identifier; branches and commits in the fork may evolve independently and never write back to the source repository. A 鈥渃lone page entry鈥?is a rea"
      },
      {
