        "text": "\"description\": \"This feature builds on the persisted objects, opened pages, or authenticated-session context provided by REQ-1-1-2 (Sign In with an Existing Account); it must reuse that context and keep pages and data consistent after the context changes. The signed-in workspace provides a 鈥淣ew repository鈥?link. The form labels are 鈥淥wner鈥? 鈥淩epository name鈥? and 鈥淒escription鈥? the signed-in user's personal namespace is selected by default, so it is possible to submit without changing the owner."
      },
      {
        "location": "applications/github/.haiknow/acceptance.json:9832",
        "text": "\"description\": \"The source overview has a button 鈥淔ork鈥? The fork form contains a field labeled 鈥淩epository name鈥?and button 鈥淐reate fork鈥? it defaults to the signed-in user's personal namespace and an allowed visibility, permitting submission after editing only the name. Seed data supplies a readable source, a user allowed to create personal repositories, and an existing fork name in that namespace for the conflict case. Success opens a heading containing the new fork name and visible text 鈥淔or"
      },
      {
        "location": "applications/github/.haiknow/acceptance.json:9927",
        "text": "\"description\": \"The 鈥渃ommit history鈥?page displays commit records for a branch or file path in reverse chronological order; the 鈥渄iff鈥?page compares the file contents of two commits or revisions line by line, where base is the earlier or target revision and compare is the newer or to-be-compared revision; the 鈥渃ode search鈥?page searches for keywords only within readable file content in the current repository. All three are read-only views that do not create commits or modify files or branches an"
      },
      {
        "location": "applications/github/.haiknow/acceptance.json:9994",
        "text": "\"description\": \"The branch selector is the control at the top of the Code page that lists and switches branches; the system stores a unique name and current pointed-to commit for each branch. Creating a branch creates a new named reference at a specified base commit; it does not copy files or rewrite base history. The default branch is the branch read by default when opening the repository overview or a repository entry without a specified branch; it is not the only existing or writable branch. "
      },
      {
        "location": "applications/github/.haiknow/acceptance.json:10518",
        "text": "\"description\": \"On an eligible PR, Merge pull request and then Confirm merge are buttons; confirming displays Merged, and that state remains after reload. A blocked PR keeps a visible disabled Merge pull request button and explains its unmet review or protection condition before any click. Seed data supplies a Maintain account and separate Open PRs for success and refusal. The eligible PR targets protected main, has a current non-author approval and test: success, and has no conflicts. The block"
      },
